## 6. Quick Exercise

Create a new annotation `@Todo` that can be applied to **methods** only, is kept in source only, and has a single element `value` containing a short description. Annotate a method with it, compile, and then use a simple IDE search or Javadoc to see the comment. Because it is `SOURCE`‑only, it will **not** be visible at runtime.

```java
import java.lang.annotation.*;

@Retention(RetentionPolicy.SOURCE)
@Target(ElementType.METHOD)
public @interface Todo {
    String value();
}
```

```java
public class Example {
    @Todo("Finish the implementation")
    public void unfinishedMethod() {
        // TODO: …
    }
}
```

